record.field:
Draft a professional email.
If the request references an Odoo record, read that record first, then read its conversation history to understand what has already been communicated before drafting. Write a clear subject line, a concise body (no filler), and an appropriate sign-off. Match the tone to the context: formal for clients or suppliers, friendly for internal colleagues.
Request: {prompt}

Summarize the content below concisely.
If the content references an Odoo record, read that record first, then read its conversation history — the discussion thread is often the most important part to summarize. Use bullet points for key information. Highlight decisions made and action items (with owners if mentioned). Keep it under 150 words unless the content is very long.
Content: {prompt}

Translate the text below. If no target language is specified, translate to English.
If the input references an Odoo record, read the record first and translate its most relevant text field (description, notes, or body). Preserve the original meaning, tone, and formatting exactly. Do not add comments or explanations.
Text: {prompt}

Proofread and improve the text below.
If the input references an Odoo record, read the record first and proofread its most relevant text field (description, notes, or body). Fix grammar, spelling, and punctuation. Improve clarity and flow where needed. Preserve the original meaning and voice. Output the improved version only — no explanations.
Text: {prompt}
